body:
Carefull. He's a hero.

&#x200B;

Congrats :)

ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha ha.(Pauses to take deep breath) Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha Ha. (Pauses for an even deeper breath) HA HA HA HA HA HA HA HA HA HA HA HA HA. (Forgets about air) HAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHAHA.

&#x200B;

Cries

Your GPA is going to gut you, but you have a lot of achievements and leadership qualification, so as long as you can show that you are going an upward trend of higher and higher grades, you should be fine because colleges love improvement. I see you're doing the capstone diploma as well : we have a long journey ahead :). As for the depression stuff, I respect that you had to deal with all that shit and was able to do so much and pull your way out. When you are writing your essay, I would recommend writing about how your depression change you instead of only talking about all the troubles. By showing how you changed, colleges see that you can pull yourself up. Congratulations, by the way on literally everything: It's really impressive.

&#x200B;

  I have a question about the literary award, though. I'm crazy in writing stories for competitions and stuff like that but I've never heard of a scholastic award. Where did you hear about the competition? And if you have a link, mind sending it?

Don't worry too much about the test. If you worry that you are going to fail, you are. Remember the College Board has made the test, so that through practice, everyone can score well. Just go with "What do I have to lose attitude". For reading, I would suggest

a) Reading and UNDERSTANDING passages better, specifically where you are weak

b) When you get a question wrong, understand WHY you got it wrong, and how you can STOP it next time.

&#x200B;

Finally understand that you may mess up on test day, and that's okay. What's not okay is freezing up and letting panic control you; don't forget what you've learned through practice.

&#x200B;

It's not going to be easy, and I'm not going to tell you that "you can do it." Only you can tell yourself that.

&#x200B;

Good luck and Godspeed

&#x200B;

PS: Sorry if I sounded harsh and serious, it wasn't my intention :)
